# Task I: DSP sample phase. LakeSnes runs a whole DSP sample (all eight voices,
# ENDX/ENVX updates, KON/KOFF) on one SPC cycle out of every 32, at cycles
# 0, 32, 64... after reset. bsnes (blargg's DSP) spreads that work over the 32
# cycles, so the point where the sound driver sees a voice-end (ENDX, read
# every tick at SPC $0976) or a key-on take effect falls a few cycles later.
# TLK's driver changes how long its tick runs on those flags, and that decides
# the latency of CPU sound commands ($C22388) and with it lag frames (6987M
# poll 1738: command acknowledged after 3548 vs 7088 master clocks in bsnes).
# Starting the counter at 25 runs each DSP sample on cycle 7 mod 32.
#
# Task DSP: 25 is derived from bsnes v115 power-on, not fitted. In bsnes the
# SMP and DSP leave reset together: SMP::power (sfc/smp/smp.cpp:40) starts at
# the IPL vector with no reset delay, DSP::power zeroes dsp.clock
# (sfc/dsp/dsp.cpp:50) and SPC_DSP::reset sets m.phase = 0
# (sfc/dsp/SPC_DSP.cpp:872). Every SMP bus cycle first calls SMP::step
# (sfc/smp/timing.cpp:35), which runs spc_dsp.run(1) via synchronizeDSP
# (sfc/smp/smp.cpp:15, sfc/dsp/dsp.cpp:12), i.e. one DSP phase per SPC cycle:
# SMP cycle j runs DSP phase j mod 32, so a DSP sample period starts (phase 0)
# on SMP cycles 0, 32, 64... LakeSnes' apu_reset instead sets
# cpuCyclesLeft = 7 (snesrecomp/runner/src/snes/apu.c:61): the SPC idles 7
# cycles before its first opcode, so bsnes SMP cycle j is our APU cycle j + 7.
# Keeping the DSP sample on phase 0 of the SMP's own timeline therefore puts it
# on our cycle 7 mod 32: (start + 7) & 31 == 0, start = 25. This agrees with
# the earlier measurement: 25 was the only start value that kept all four TAS
# replays in sync; 24 and 26 desync 6987M/6781M/4735M at poll 1785, 27/28/31
# desync 2716M at poll 1775 (INTEGRATE.md).
@@ apu-dsp-sample-phase
<<<<
  apu->dspAdr = 0;
  apu->cycles = 0;
====
  apu->dspAdr = 0;
  apu->cycles = 25;  /* bsnes DSP phase 0 = SMP cycle 0 = our cycle 7 (7-cycle reset delay) */
  { const char *e = getenv("TLK_DSP_PHASE"); if (e) apu->cycles = (uint64_t)strtoul(e, NULL, 10); }  /* Task O: experiments */
>>>>
